// `#[derive(Copy, Clone)]` on a struct with an array field needs a Copy element type:
// `[Token; 2]` is not Copy (E0204, Sabiko's E0417) and not Clone either (E0277 from the
// `Clone` derive), both reported at the struct, so this is not a differential program.
// An array of a Copy type is fine (run/arrays/copy_semantics.sabi).
struct Token { Id: i32 }

#[derive(Copy, Clone)]
struct Hand { Cards: [Token; 2] } //~ rustc E0204: the trait `Copy` cannot be implemented for this type //~ rustc E0277: the trait bound `Token: Clone` is not satisfied [the trait `Clone` is not implemented for `Token`]
